# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal research and strategy. NEVER commit these.
#
# The build constitution and the research hauls are internal working documents.
# Publishing them would leak strategy, competitor analysis, and third-party
# contact details into a public repo. Gitignored before `git init` on purpose:
# untracked is not protection, and one reflexive `git add -A` is the whole
# distance between local and published.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pdf
!docs/**/*.pdf
CLAUDE*.md
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md
VERIFICATION_FINDINGS*
Curtail_Mobile_Layer_Spec*
_research/
_private/
_plan/

# Third-party reference material. This is another company's proprietary
# minified bundle, studied for motion patterns and never redistributed.
noomo-showcase-frontend.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Cardinal rule: never commit one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
service-account*.json
gha-creds-*.json
.npmrc
.pypirc
application_default_credentials.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# JavaScript / TypeScript
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/
build/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
.pnpm-store/
coverage/

# Service worker output, generated from app/sw.ts at build time
public/sw.js
public/sw.js.map
public/workbox-*.js
public/swe-worker-*.js

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
.tox/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Infrastructure
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
crash.log
# .gcloudignore is TRACKED, deliberately, and it was ignored here by default.
#
# It is a safety control rather than local scratch: it keeps the gitignored corpus
# of government PDFs and the internal strategy folder out of the Cloud Run build
# context, so neither can end up inside a container image pushed to a registry. A
# control that lives only on one machine protects only that machine, and the next
# person to deploy from a fresh clone would have shipped both.
# !.gcloudignore

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test and capture artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/
.playwright/
*.webm
*.mp4
*.mov
!docs/media/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data. The order corpus and gage snapshots are fetched, not vendored.
# Cached responses can be large and are reproducible from public sources.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/cache/
data/corpus/**/*.pdf
data/snapshots/
*.pmtiles
*.mbtiles

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS and editor
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local agent tooling. Project-scoped Claude settings stay local.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
.serena/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Android signing material. A keystore is a credential with a password, and a leaked
# one lets somebody ship an update that Android trusts as us.
*.keystore
*.jks
twa-manifest.json
android/

# The Xcode project is GENERATED from ios/project.yml by xcodegen. A pbxproj is 300
# lines of UUID-laden plist that no reviewer can read and every merge conflicts on, so
# the declaration is committed and the artifact is not.
ios/*.xcodeproj/
ios/build/
ios/DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
*.ipa
*.dSYM.zip
